+## 3. PASS 2 — QUALITY
+
+### 3.1 Code quality
+
+Clean. The two structures that could have gone wrong did not: `routed_job` is a
+copy so the manifest dict the digest pins is never mutated, and `TIER_RAISE` is an
+independent ascending table rather than arithmetic on the descending `TIERS`
+list — the exact defect pre-flight 1A warned about. `run_recall_check` has a
+single exit shape and cannot raise: every branch returns a dict. Failure notes
+carry the engine's own `rc` and stderr (truncated at 200 chars), so an unavailable
+verdict is diagnosable instead of merely sad.
+
+One note, not a defect: `recall_check_file` is set only for a `tighten` verdict,
+so a `none` job writes no artefact and its `register-lane` line stays as it was —
+the run directory does not fill with empty verdicts.
+
+### 3.2 No regression
+
+With `auto_tighten` false (the default, and the state of every existing manifest)
+`routed_job is job` and `entry_tier == job.get("tier")`, so routing is bit-for-bit
+what it was. The three `resolve_job_model` / `build_launch_argv` call sites all
+moved to `routed_job` together — no caller left on the old variable.
+
+```
+$ /usr/bin/python3 -B scripts/compound-v-emit-workflow.py --selftest
+491/491 checks passed
+$ bash tests/test-engine-c-contract.sh
+✅ engine-c contract: every generated job_result conforms, the contract reaches the worker, and the join has a producer
+$ /usr/bin/python3 -B scripts/lint-frontmatter.py .
+✅ All frontmatter clean
+```
+
+### 3.3 Test alignment
+
+Every MUST has a guard. The new block (`selftest`, `scripts/compound-v-emit-workflow.py:8095-8305`) asserts: the verdict and its exact
+match count from a temp results root; the ≤3 evidence cap; `none` on a clean lane;
+the prompt section and the `--recall-check-json` hand-back; their **absence** on a
+clean lane; the tier untouched without `auto_tighten`; the one-rung raise; that the
+**resolver** receives the raised tier (pinned against `resolve_job_model(tier=standard)`
+rather than against "different from unraised", which would false-fail on a routing
+table where two tiers share a model); the explicit-`model:` carve-out; the review
+clause; the `TIER_RAISE` shape; `--no-recall`; missing engine; rc≠0 engine;
+non-JSON engine; timeout-and-kill; `register-lane` writing state.json; junk input
+not stopping registration; and an end-to-end `cmd_emit` that checks the artefact
+and the emitted script.
+
+The one requirement with **no** guard is the spec's reading-budget wording — because
+it was not implemented (ISSUE 1).
+
+### 3.4 No fabricated metrics
+
+None. `recall_check_ms` is a real `time.monotonic()` delta (`:1307`). The CHANGELOG's
+only number, "7 of the 27 runs dispatched today", is the spec's own probe result.
+No hardcoded baseline, no savings meter, no invented percentage anywhere in the diff.
+
+### 3.5 No reward-hacking
+
+The selftest block is **additive**: no `_check` was removed, renamed, skipped or
+loosened; no threshold moved; no test file deleted. Count rose to 491/491. The one
+place a gate could have been weakened — asserting the raise by comparing resolved
+models — was deliberately made *stronger* by pinning the resolver's expected output
+instead (comment at `:8172-8176`). §2.6 does not apply: this is not a marathon run
+and there is no `blocked_external` verdict in it.
